1
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:47,400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The consultation of the Committee on Finance, Subcommittee A, with civil society organizations to discuss budgetary priorities for the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget is hereby called to order. I'd like to acknowledge the presence of our colleague, Senator Panfilo Lacson.

2
00:31:48,800 --> 00:32:13,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And before we recognize the resource persons, the Chair would like to state some guidelines for our orderly conduct for this afternoon. Due to the limited number of seats available at the panel, only one resource person per CSO will be seated at the panel. Should a question be addressed or answered by your colleague, you must first seek the permission of the Chair to have your colleague recognized before they may respond.

3
00:32:14,280 --> 00:32:48,140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We would like also to remind everyone that each CSO is allotted a maximum of five minutes to deliver its statement or presentation. A timer will be displayed on the screen to help everyone keep track of their allotted time. Thank you for your understanding and cooperation. We welcome our partners from civil society organizations and all our guests for today's discussions. At this juncture, may I request the Committee Secretary to acknowledge the resource persons present for today.

4
00:32:48,740 --> 00:33:03,020
Committee Secretary: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Good afternoon. Good afternoon also to Senator Lacson. For the consultation with civil society organizations to discuss budgetary priorities for the FY 2027 General Appropriations Act or GAA, we would like to acknowledge our resource persons.

5
00:33:03,020 --> 00:33:37,560
Committee Secretary: First, from the People's Budget Coalition, we have Mr. Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante together with Ms. Zy-za Nadine Suzara, Mr. Adolfo Jose Montesa and Ms. Maxine Valdez. For GoodGovPH, we have Mr. Michel Andre Macahilo. From Social Watch Philippines, we have Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza, who is also a professor of UP NCPAG, together with Mr. Alci Kitalig and Ms. Desiree Peña-Flor. From the Caucus of Development NGO Networks or CODE-NGO, we have Ms. Catherine Basalote together with Ms. Samantha May Santos and Mr. Lawrence Kenneth Castillo.

6
