01:11:42,160 --> 01:11:44,440
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: so it's incomplete at the end of the day.

671
01:11:44,440 --> 01:11:47,160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Or in existing documents, it's oversimplified

672
01:11:47,160 --> 01:11:48,480
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: or it comes in passing.

673
01:11:48,480 --> 01:11:50,720
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Therefore, these programs are heavily insulated

674
01:11:50,720 --> 01:11:52,280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: from public scrutiny.

675
01:11:52,280 --> 01:11:55,160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Also, recent incidents of school-based violence

676
01:11:55,160 --> 01:11:58,320
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: across the country highlight the need for avenues for healthy,

677
01:11:58,320 --> 01:12:01,840
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: socialization, instilling of positive values

678
01:12:01,840 --> 01:12:04,680
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and cultivation of love of community and country.

679
01:12:04,680 --> 01:12:06,160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: We respectfully ask, therefore,

680
01:12:06,160 --> 01:12:09,600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: the Senate Committee on Finance for these specific measures.

681
01:12:09,600 --> 01:12:13,480
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: First, it's to increase DepEd, BLS, and YFD budget

682
01:12:13,480 --> 01:12:15,440
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: by at least P250 million.

683
01:12:15,440 --> 01:12:17,640
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: This is so the Bureau can fund the following.

684
01:12:17,640 --> 01:12:20,200
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: The institutionalization of after-school programs,

685
01:12:20,200 --> 01:12:23,600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: clubs, and organizations so that the DepEd can also do things

686
01:12:23,600 --> 01:12:25,200
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: like review of the policy framework

687
01:12:25,200 --> 01:12:28,280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: on the after-school co-curricular and extracurricular programs.

688
01:12:28,320 --> 01:12:31,120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Secondly, it's to strengthen learner governments

689
01:12:31,120 --> 01:12:33,600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: as a civic education engagement platform.

690
01:12:33,600 --> 01:12:35,960
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: That is to say, they will do things like consultations,

691
01:12:35,960 --> 01:12:38,440
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: policy discussions, and policy validation.

692
01:12:38,440 --> 01:12:41,280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Third is to strengthen the career guidance program

693
01:12:41,280 --> 01:12:44,640
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and ensure these programs are written as separate line items

694
01:12:44,640 --> 01:12:49,000
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: to guarantee appropriate funding for these programs

695
01:12:49,000 --> 01:12:50,840
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: so that they are able to be scrutinized

696
01:12:50,840 --> 01:12:53,120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: in cases where budget's insufficient.

697
01:12:53,120 --> 01:12:56,160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: To quote EDCOM 2's report on the Filipino learner today,

698
01:12:56,160 --> 01:12:57,360
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: when adequately...

699
01:12:58,320 --> 01:12:59,480
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: When adequately supported,

700
01:12:59,480 --> 01:13:02,120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: this becomes programs, laboratories rather,

701
01:13:02,120 --> 01:13:05,320
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: of participation where students deliberate on shared issues,

702
01:13:05,320 --> 01:13:07,840
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: organize initiatives, and experience responsibility

703
01:13:07,840 --> 01:13:09,280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: for collective outcomes.

704
01:13:09,280 --> 01:13:12,280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Education for citizenship as articulated in young people

705
01:13:12,280 --> 01:13:15,120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: learning to become active citizens is most effective

706
01:13:15,120 --> 01:13:17,080
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: when it allows the youth to learn, participate,

707
01:13:17,080 --> 01:13:18,760
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and reflect and lead within communities

708
01:13:18,760 --> 01:13:20,080
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: that value their voice.

709
01:13:20,080 --> 01:13:22,520
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: We therefore urge the Senate to act on these measures

710
01:13:22,520 --> 01:13:23,720
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: for the Filipino youth,

711
01:13:23,720 --> 01:13:25,600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and to ensure that their learning is holistic

712
01:13:25,600 --> 01:13:27,120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and goes beyond the classroom,

713
01:13:27,120 --> 01:13:28,160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: which allows them to have access

714
01:13:28,160 --> 01:13:30,960
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: to pathways of sustainable outlets and alternatives

715
01:13:30,960 --> 01:13:32,880
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: compared to the prevailing culture now

716
01:13:32,880 --> 01:13:34,280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: where they are nudged to isolation

717
01:13:34,280 --> 01:13:36,600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: because of a lack of access to these programs.

718
01:13:36,600 --> 01:13:39,120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Learner governments and school-based organizations

719
01:13:39,120 --> 01:13:40,920
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: offer young people opportunities

720
01:13:40,920 --> 01:13:42,960
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: to kickstart their respective leadership journeys.

721
01:13:42,960 --> 01:13:45,920
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Learner governments and clubs can train people in leadership,

722
01:13:45,920 --> 01:13:48,880
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: civic engagement, and advocacy in their purpose,

723
01:13:48,880 --> 01:13:51,840
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: which are crucial for leading youth governance institutions

724
01:13:51,840 --> 01:13:53,800
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: in preparing for public leadership.

725
01:13:53,800 --> 01:13:56,000
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Again, from GoodGov PH,

726
01:13:56,000 --> 01:13:58,000
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: maraming salamat at mabuhay ang kabataang Pilipino.

727
01:13:58,160 --> 01:13:59,160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Thank you.

728
01:13:59,160 --> 01:14:00,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

729
01:14:00,160 --> 01:14:03,000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mr. Michelle Macahilo, next.

730
01:14:03,000 --> 01:14:06,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: On the list is Social Watch Philippines

731
01:14:06,320 --> 01:14:08,040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and NCPAG-UP,

732
01:14:08,040 --> 01:14:10,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza,

733
01:14:10,800 --> 01:14:14,080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: co-convenor of Social Watch.

734
01:14:14,080 --> 01:14:15,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: You have the floor.

735
01:14:15,640 --> 01:14:17,200
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Thank you.

736
01:14:17,200 --> 01:14:18,640
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Good afternoon.

737
01:14:18,640 --> 01:14:21,320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: On behalf of Social Watch Philippines,

738
01:14:21,320 --> 01:14:23,560
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: I will present our assessment of the proposed

739
01:14:23,560 --> 01:14:28,000
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: 2027 Budget to the Lens of Social Equity and Human Rights.

740
01:14:28,160 --> 01:14:32,760
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: My colleagues around the table will subsequently elaborate

741
01:14:32,760 --> 01:14:34,920
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: on our findings and recommendations.

742
01:14:34,920 --> 01:14:37,320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: So, viewed through this lens,

743
01:14:37,320 --> 01:14:43,320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: the proposed 2027 budget raises a number of serious concerns.

744
01:14:43,320 --> 01:14:49,320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: First, the apparent failure to prioritize the productive sectors,

745
01:14:49,320 --> 01:14:53,600
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: particularly agriculture, trade, and industry,

746
01:14:53,600 --> 01:14:57,800
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: which historically has been getting very low public investments,

747
01:14:58,160 --> 01:14:59,960
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and it is even lower this year.

748
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:07,740
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: These are critical to raising productivity, generating decent employment, and improving people's incomes.

749
01:15:07,740 --> 01:15:22,340
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The 2027 proposed budget raises debt service, public works, the defense sector, law and order, while significantly cutting the budget for agriculture, agrarian reform, and trade and industry.

750
01:15:22,340 --> 01:15:31,740
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: These are the productivity-enhancing sectors, the productivity-enhancing agencies that promote people's incomes, people's livelihoods, and employments.

751
01:15:32,380 --> 01:15:45,460
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This tilts the budget towards fiscal obligations, infrastructure, defense, and law and order, and these are prioritized over enhancing productivity and increasing incomes for our people.

752
01:15:45,940 --> 01:15:47,520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This must be addressed.

753
01:15:47,520 --> 01:15:51,520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: We are very, very disturbed by the lack of prioritization.

754
01:15:52,340 --> 01:16:01,800
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: We are very, very disturbed by the lack of prioritization of productivity-enhancing economic activities which our people badly need, particularly in agriculture and MSMEs.

755
01:16:02,520 --> 01:16:07,020
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Second, so basically this imbalance raises a fundamental question.

756
01:16:07,020 --> 01:16:20,060
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: How can we aspire to inclusive development without adequately investing in the productive capacities that enable Filipinos to secure decent work and lift themselves outside of poverty?

757
01:16:20,500 --> 01:16:22,120
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This is a structural transformation.

758
01:16:22,920 --> 01:16:25,620
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: If we talk systemic, this is systemic.

759
01:16:26,880 --> 01:16:31,220
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Second, now we'll talk about human development.

760
01:16:32,060 --> 01:16:38,960
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The relegation of people's well-being, dignity, and human development has also been relegated to a secondary concern.

761
01:16:39,720 --> 01:16:52,320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Infrastructure and debt service received the highest budgetary increases, while significant budget cuts have yet again been made to health, education, housing, and other essential social needs.

762
01:16:52,340 --> 01:16:59,480
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Now, this raises budgetary issues about the kinds of priorities of our policymakers.

763
01:17:00,460 --> 01:17:10,400
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: I'm sorry to say, are we building the foundations for lasting human development, or are we merely managing the consequences of persistent poverty and inequality?

764
01:17:10,900 --> 01:17:16,720
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This is very residual social policy rather than transformative.

765
01:17:16,720 --> 01:17:22,140
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Third, and perhaps most troubling, is the persistence.

766
01:17:22,340 --> 01:17:32,540
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This is the result of appropriations vulnerable to pork barrel and patronage politics, which our colleagues in People's Budget Coalition have already very much focused on.

767
01:17:32,540 --> 01:17:45,560
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Our analysis identifies ₱221 billion of DPWH's BIP program in the House-approved budget, ₱72 billion above the proposed NEP allocation.

768
01:17:46,340 --> 01:17:52,040
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: These practices are especially troubling in light of the Supreme Court's recent ruling.

769
01:17:52,040 --> 01:18:06,380
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This problem of political discretion, now we go to soft pork, extends to social protection programs, which are indispensable in a country marked by widespread poverty and inequality.

770
01:18:07,220 --> 01:18:16,220
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The House-approved GAB also contains what may be characterized as soft pork, and our colleagues in PBC have mentioned this in a very thorough way.

771
01:18:16,220 --> 01:18:21,220
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: At the very least, we urge the Senate to restore their allocations.

772
01:18:22,040 --> 01:18:28,340
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to the NEP level, and the freed-up resources go to [unclear]. I will talk about that later in the recommendations.

773
01:18:28,340 --> 01:18:35,680
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: But let us be clear, the problem is not social protection itself, but its appropriation for political ends.

774
01:18:37,020 --> 01:18:42,920
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: So consider PhilHealth and MAIFIP, and my colleagues will talk about this much more extensively.

775
01:18:42,920 --> 01:18:49,920
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: May pakalakang papel naman ang MAIFIP bilang safety net para sa mga pasyenteng kulang ang health coverage.

776
01:18:50,040 --> 01:18:52,320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Ngunit meron na tayong PhilHealth eh.

777
01:18:53,040 --> 01:19:02,060
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Sa ilalim ng Universal Health Care Act, hindi dapat maging permanenteng kapalit ng PhilHealth sa isang parallel system ng medical assistance.

778
01:19:02,480 --> 01:19:07,040
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Kung kulang ang benepisyon ng PhilHealth sa tamang tugon, ito kasi ng PhilHealth.

779
01:19:08,000 --> 01:19:10,040
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Hindi patuloy napalakihin ang MAIFIP.

780
01:19:10,040 --> 01:19:19,440
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Yet in the proposed 2027 budget, PhilHealth remains inadequately funded to fulfill its universal mandate.

781
01:19:20,040 --> 01:19:26,380
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: While MAIFIP retains substantial allocations, which we all know is vulnerable to patronage politics.

782
01:19:27,520 --> 01:19:32,780
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Napakasakit ang isang Pilipino, hindi niya dapat itanong, sino ang malalipitan ko?

783
01:19:33,500 --> 01:19:37,600
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Ang dapat niyang sasabihin, covered ako, karapatan ko to.

784
01:19:38,400 --> 01:19:46,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Now to LGSF, which stands at 62.62 billion from the HGAB, as we know, is also a kind of pork barrel,

785
01:19:46,940 --> 01:19:51,120
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: especially the FALBU, the SBDP, and the DRR Assistance Program.

786
01:19:51,660 --> 01:19:53,520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: These are all discretionary funds, no?

787
01:19:54,060 --> 01:19:56,420
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: And are highly vulnerable to patronage politics.

788
01:19:56,920 --> 01:19:59,720
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: And let's face it, especially as 2028 nears.

789
01:20:01,100 --> 01:20:08,320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Adding soft pork, so if we add soft pork that I talked about earlier with the hard pork of BIP and LGSF,

790
01:20:08,320 --> 01:20:14,640
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: we at least identified about 427 billion in appropriations that warrant rigorous scrutiny

791
01:20:14,640 --> 01:20:16,760
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: because of their extreme vulnerability.

792
01:20:16,940 --> 01:20:19,880
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to political patronage and corruption.

793
01:20:19,880 --> 01:20:22,740
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: So this brings us to a fundamental question.

794
01:20:23,240 --> 01:20:26,160
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Whose interest does our national budget ultimately serve?

795
01:20:26,520 --> 01:20:29,280
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The Filipino people or those who wield political power?

796
01:20:30,180 --> 01:20:37,500
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: We cannot ignore the still unresolved flood control corruption scandal involving hundreds of billions of pesos.

797
01:20:38,160 --> 01:20:41,520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: It remains an open wound in our national consciousness,

798
01:20:42,180 --> 01:20:45,440
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: compounded by the continuing absence of meaningful accountability.

799
01:20:46,940 --> 01:20:49,260
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The Filipino people have not forgotten.

800
01:20:50,000 --> 01:20:55,520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The recent Supreme Court rulings have reinforced long-standing civil society concerns

801
01:20:55,520 --> 01:21:03,060
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: over unconstitutional budgetary practices, including unlawful congressional increases in appropriations,

802
01:21:03,620 --> 01:21:06,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: weakened safeguards over universal appropriations,

803
01:21:07,400 --> 01:21:12,000
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: prohibited lump-sum appropriations that enable discretionary project allocations,

804
01:21:12,400 --> 01:21:13,780
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: including for flood control.

805
01:21:13,780 --> 01:21:16,780
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: As our committee chair,

806
01:21:16,940 --> 01:21:17,800
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: has said,

807
01:21:18,160 --> 01:21:21,480
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: these revelations have profoundly eroded public trust,

808
01:21:21,960 --> 01:21:25,440
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: fueling deep anger and a sense of betrayal.

809
01:21:26,380 --> 01:21:29,360
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: As such, it is with a sense of urgency that we call on the Senate

810
01:21:29,360 --> 01:21:32,160
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to undertake five decisive actions.

811
01:21:32,640 --> 01:21:38,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: First, scrutinize and remove the estimated 427 billion in appropriations vulnerable to hard and soft pork.

812
01:21:39,360 --> 01:21:40,640
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Mas malaki yung sa PBC.

813
01:21:41,740 --> 01:21:43,120
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Dapat isama talaga yan.

814
01:21:43,120 --> 01:21:45,120
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Second,

815
01:21:46,940 --> 01:21:48,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: redirect these resources towards agriculture,

816
01:21:48,940 --> 01:21:50,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: trade and industry

817
01:21:50,940 --> 01:21:52,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to raise productivity,

818
01:21:52,940 --> 01:21:54,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: generate decent work,

819
01:21:54,940 --> 01:21:56,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and strengthen sustainable employment and livelihoods.

820
01:21:56,940 --> 01:21:58,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The most sustainable pathway out of poverty is decent work.

821
01:22:00,940 --> 01:22:02,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Let's put decent work up in the agenda.

822
01:22:04,940 --> 01:22:06,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Third,

823
01:22:06,940 --> 01:22:08,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: increase investments in education,

824
01:22:08,940 --> 01:22:10,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: health, housing,

825
01:22:10,940 --> 01:22:12,940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: social protection, child protection,

