03:02:59,960 --> 03:03:06,180
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Nakakalungkot kasi tumaas man ang budget ng DSWD pero napunta sa AICS.

3895
03:03:06,900 --> 03:03:10,980
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Hindi po natin tinatahinggihan ng ayuda pero mas gusto po namin yung long term.

3896
03:03:11,560 --> 03:03:18,080
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Hindi rin po namin gusto na magkasakit at syempre magmakaawa sa ating mga binoboto.

3897
03:03:18,940 --> 03:03:21,080
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Malinaw na malinaw po sa aming mga kaisipan.

3898
03:03:21,820 --> 03:03:26,420
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Na hindi naman talaga dapat privilege ito. Karapatan po ito.

3899
03:03:26,860 --> 03:03:32,900
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Sabi nga natin kung gusto talaga natin mabawasan ang mahihirap, kunseryoso po tayo dito,

3900
03:03:33,240 --> 03:03:36,820
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: bigyan natin mga long term na mga proyekto, programa.

3901
03:03:37,700 --> 03:03:44,680
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: At syempre po, kailangan din natin na tulungan kami dahil si SNPP po ay mga volunteer na leader.

3902
03:03:45,280 --> 03:03:49,820
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Nagkakandak po kami monthly na hindi bababa sa apat na mga meetings po

3903
03:03:49,820 --> 03:03:53,380
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: para magbahagi mga musta sa kapwa namin may hirap.

3904
03:03:53,960 --> 03:03:59,900
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: At ganun din po kalampagin sila na hindi lang dapat tayo umaasa, nagbibinipisyo,

3905
03:03:59,900 --> 03:04:08,220
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: kundi dapat kasama tayo sa pagbuo ng mga pulisiya na makakatulong sa pagtaas o antas ng ating pamumuhay.

3906
03:04:08,720 --> 03:04:16,660
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Dahil mahirap po maging aasa ka lang dahil hindi po totoo na ang pantawid o mga purpose po ay mga tamad.

3907
03:04:17,100 --> 03:04:19,800
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Siguro po, hindi man perfecto pero may ilan.

3908
03:04:19,820 --> 03:04:30,620
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Talaga po hindi natin basta-basta madadaan sa mga FTS pero marami pa rin po mga katulad ng SNPP na nais pa rin po makatulong

3909
03:04:30,620 --> 03:04:38,820
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: dahil nakikita po natin na itong mga programa katulad po ngayon kami po talaga ay nangangamba

3910
03:04:38,820 --> 03:04:46,500
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: dahil alam naman po natin na ang inflation ay patuloy na nanaranasan ng bawat isa lalo na po itong El Niño.

3911
03:04:46,760 --> 03:04:49,500
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Sabi nga, dahil nga sa...

3912
03:04:49,820 --> 03:04:55,180
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Sa paghihigpit ng sinturon, hindi na po namin alam kung paano pa namin hihigpitan eh.

3913
03:04:56,220 --> 03:04:57,300
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Paano pang pagtitipid.

3914
03:04:57,420 --> 03:05:06,220
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Sana po hindi rin matulad ang purpose doon sa hindi makataong pagtitipid na nararanasan.

3915
03:05:06,480 --> 03:05:16,300
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Sana mabigyan po ng final version na mas maganda ang budget ng bawat ahensya na makakatulong sa pag-alibid po ng mga mahihirap.

3916
03:05:17,100 --> 03:05:19,300
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Umaasa po kami sa Senado.

3917
03:05:19,820 --> 03:05:31,280
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Sa mga Senador na aming mga nakakausap, lalong-lalong na po nagpapasalamat ako dahil isa po kami sa SNPP na miyembro po ng kwalisyon ng People's Budget Coalition

3918
03:05:31,280 --> 03:05:39,740
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: na ilan taon na rin po kami nangangalampag para tumulong at pinagmamalakay ko rin po na ang samahan na kakaisang pamilyang pantawid

3919
03:05:39,740 --> 03:05:48,460
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: hindi lang po umaasa sa ayuda dahil isa na rin po kaming mga citizens monitor kasi alam na rin po namin kung ano po yung TPA.

3920
03:05:48,460 --> 03:05:49,460
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Kaya sana...

3921
03:05:49,820 --> 03:05:59,540
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Kasama ninyo kami at sasama nyo kami sa lahat ng mga usapin tungkol po sa ating mga pagbabudget po.

3922
03:06:00,180 --> 03:06:15,840
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: At umaasa rin po kami na ang budget po na final version ay magkakaroon ng maganda-gandang numero para naman po mag-reflect po sa edukasyon, sa nutrisyon at sa siyempre po sa health po.

3923
03:06:15,840 --> 03:06:18,840
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: At alam naman po natin na habang...

3924
03:06:19,820 --> 03:06:25,320
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Ang mga estudyante sa 4Ps ay lumalaki rin po ang gastusin lalo na po yung mga senior high.

3925
03:06:25,860 --> 03:06:38,820
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Pero nakakatuwa po kahit pasabihin na ito nga po talaga ay human investment no dahil mahigit 80,000 mga nakagraduate po mula po sa 4Ps ay mga professional na po ngayon.

3926
03:06:38,820 --> 03:06:47,900
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Lalo na po kung ito po ay ating mga susuportahan ng tamang budget baka hindi lang po sasabihin nyo tamad talaga ang 4Ps.

3927
03:06:48,260 --> 03:06:49,660
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Kundi isa na po silang...

3928
03:06:49,660 --> 03:06:54,240
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Kaharap natin na nagboboses bilang advocate po.

3929
03:06:54,640 --> 03:06:56,200
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Kaya maasa po kami.

3930
03:06:56,840 --> 03:06:57,920
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Talagang nangungulit.

3931
03:06:58,400 --> 03:07:08,920
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: At natutuwa po ako sa narinig ko kanina kay Sen. JB at Sen. Ping na makasama rin po sana kami sa BICAM po.

3932
03:07:09,460 --> 03:07:14,340
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Kanina nagtawa nang kami ni Ken kasi sabi namin parang ang sarap magdala ng scorecard.

3933
03:07:14,560 --> 03:07:18,120
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Meron pong sad, may happy, may ganun po, may pahart.

3934
03:07:18,620 --> 03:07:19,480
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Para naman po.

3935
03:07:19,660 --> 03:07:30,380
SNPP National President Annabelle Luna: Baka maka-apekto ito sa pag-iisip ng ating mga legislator na magbigay ng mahusay at makataong budget. Maraming salamat po.

3936
03:07:31,240 --> 03:07:32,040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Wang.

3937
03:07:32,700 --> 03:07:33,480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Isana Beluna.

3938
03:07:34,680 --> 03:07:39,660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next, Miss Pauline Navarro from...

3939
03:07:39,660 --> 03:07:41,880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: World Vision.

3940
03:07:42,980 --> 03:07:44,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: World Vision Philippines.

3941
03:07:44,800 --> 03:07:47,520
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Yan po. Magandang hapon po sa ating lahat.

3942
03:07:47,780 --> 03:07:49,500
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Sa mga kasamahan po natin.

3943
03:07:49,660 --> 03:07:53,000
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Sa CSOs at of course po sa ating mga Senators na nandito ngayon.

3944
03:07:53,140 --> 03:08:00,380
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, gusto ko pong simulan yung aking sharing sa pagsasabi na ang bata ang dapat bida sa budget.

3945
03:08:00,700 --> 03:08:03,700
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Lalo na po sa mga usapin na nakaka-apekto sa kanila.

3946
03:08:03,900 --> 03:08:08,200
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Yung ilan po dito nabanggit na nausapin po ng health, education.

3947
03:08:09,320 --> 03:08:13,880
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: I-emphasize ko din po yun sa child participation at of course yung child protection.

3948
03:08:15,260 --> 03:08:19,420
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: With that po, gusto ko rin pong banggitin na sa usapin ng child,

3949
03:08:19,660 --> 03:08:26,000
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: protection, marami pong mga bata ang patuloy na nakakaranas ng pang-aabuso,

3950
03:08:26,240 --> 03:08:29,040
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: ng karahasan, at na-exploitation.

3951
03:08:29,420 --> 03:08:36,760
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, may reported child abuse cases po ay equivalent sa isang bata ang naaabuso kada oras,

3952
03:08:37,480 --> 03:08:38,300
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: bawat araw.

3953
03:08:39,040 --> 03:08:43,280
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: And nearly 70% po ng mga violence against children,

3954
03:08:43,660 --> 03:08:47,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: violence cases are child sexual abuse cases.

3955
03:08:47,780 --> 03:08:49,500
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, ito po ay isang...

3956
03:08:49,660 --> 03:08:55,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Ito ay isang alarming issues po, hindi lamang po para sa ating mga nakatatanda,

3957
03:08:55,600 --> 03:08:57,060
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: pero lalo na po sa mga bata.

3958
03:08:57,260 --> 03:09:05,540
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Dahil nagkaroon po kami ng mga consultations at palagi pong ang usapin ng child sexual abuse and exploitation

3959
03:09:05,540 --> 03:09:10,340
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: ang lagi pong nangunguna sa kanilang mga concerns ng mga bata.

3960
03:09:10,900 --> 03:09:14,940
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, we acknowledge po na meron tayong significant steps.

3961
03:09:14,940 --> 03:09:19,380
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: The Philippine government has taken significant steps to strengthen po yung response,

3962
03:09:19,380 --> 03:09:20,780
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: to OSAIC and SISAEM.

3963
03:09:20,900 --> 03:09:27,580
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: We have the Republic Act No. 11930 or the Anti-OSAIC and Anti-SISAEM Act

3964
03:09:27,580 --> 03:09:29,700
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: enacted in 2022.

3965
03:09:30,000 --> 03:09:32,380
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: And of course, these commitments were further operationalized

3966
03:09:33,180 --> 03:09:37,380
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: through the Philippine Strategic Plan against OSAIC and SISAEM 2025 to 2028,

3967
03:09:38,060 --> 03:09:40,420
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: launched naman po in December 2025.

3968
03:09:41,260 --> 03:09:45,200
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, to support the implementation, the NCC OSAIC-SISAEM,

3969
03:09:45,520 --> 03:09:49,320
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Social Watch Philippines, alongside other member agencies,

3970
03:09:49,380 --> 03:09:52,980
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and CSOs, developed the Costed Implementation Plan,

3971
03:09:53,480 --> 03:09:56,460
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: translating priorities into time-bound activities,

3972
03:09:57,020 --> 03:09:59,020
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: resource requirements, and cost estimates,

3973
03:09:59,140 --> 03:10:01,180
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: aligned with the national budgeting cycle.

3974
03:10:02,120 --> 03:10:07,120
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, with this framework po, kami po sa Social Watch Philippines Alternative Budget Initiative

3975
03:10:07,120 --> 03:10:12,940
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Child Protection Cluster na binubo po ng iba't-ibang child-focused organizations.

3976
03:10:13,780 --> 03:10:17,680
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Isa po ako doon from World Vision, and of course, yung iba po pong kasama ay nandito din.

3977
03:10:18,260 --> 03:10:19,260
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: We propose,

3978
03:10:19,260 --> 03:10:24,660
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: We propose an alternative budget of 4.4 billion peso for fiscal year 2027

3979
03:10:24,660 --> 03:10:27,600
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: to strengthen the national child protection system.

3980
03:10:28,260 --> 03:10:32,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, this includes dedicated allocations for the OSAIC-SISAEM,

3981
03:10:32,600 --> 03:10:35,220
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: proper proposals across key result areas,

3982
03:10:35,500 --> 03:10:39,480
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: to fund advocacy, case management, law enforcement databases,

3983
03:10:39,800 --> 03:10:43,720
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and specialized training, amounting to 154 million pesos.

3984
03:10:44,600 --> 03:10:48,540
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, ang mga beneficiaries po nito ay mga child victim survivors,

3985
03:10:49,260 --> 03:10:53,740
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and adolescent survivors of sexual abuse, physical abuse, exploitation,

3986
03:10:54,220 --> 03:10:56,040
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: trafficking, and OSAIC and SISAEM,

3987
03:10:56,100 --> 03:11:00,100
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: as well as children requiring trauma-informed mental health care.

3988
03:11:01,040 --> 03:11:05,020
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: The proposals also emphasize meaningful child and youth participation

3989
03:11:05,020 --> 03:11:07,080
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: in prevention and response,

3990
03:11:07,580 --> 03:11:11,500
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: ensuring the solutions are child-friendly, gender-sensitive, and inclusive.

3991
03:11:13,200 --> 03:11:17,000
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: If mapaflash po yung aming presentation on this,

3992
03:11:17,000 --> 03:11:18,540
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: meron po kaming sinabmit na,

3993
03:11:19,260 --> 03:11:22,740
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: PowerPoint for our proposed budget proposals.

3994
03:11:23,400 --> 03:11:25,040
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: But, I'll go through na lang po,

3995
03:11:25,140 --> 03:11:27,380
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and hopefully may flash din po siya later,

3996
03:11:27,640 --> 03:11:29,240
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: or kung pwede na po ngayon.

3997
03:11:29,980 --> 03:11:31,860
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, for yung aming po proposal,

3998
03:11:31,860 --> 03:11:36,240
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: ay para sa iba't-ibang member agencies po ng NCCO-SAEC-SISAEM.

3999
03:11:36,320 --> 03:11:41,000
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So, we'll start po with DOJ, NCCO-SAEC Secretariat.

4000
03:11:42,760 --> 03:11:48,500
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: We're proposing po a total of,

4001
03:11:49,260 --> 03:11:52,040
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: 105 million pesos.

4002
03:11:52,260 --> 03:11:56,880
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So kasama po doon yung case management and first contact protocols

4003
03:11:56,880 --> 03:12:01,620
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: that will help standardize how frontline responders handle osaig cases

4004
03:12:01,620 --> 03:12:06,980
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: from initial contact and rescue operations to referral for appropriate care.

4005
03:12:07,900 --> 03:12:14,080
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Importante din po dito yung 90 million pesos for an integrated database and registry system.

4006
03:12:14,080 --> 03:12:19,960
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So this one po, the proposed system aims to centralize and harmonize relevant data

4007
03:12:19,960 --> 03:12:24,280
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: to support offender identification and law enforcement investigations,

4008
03:12:24,780 --> 03:12:28,220
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: as well as an additional 4 million for dedicated technical personnel

4009
03:12:28,220 --> 03:12:32,520
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: to manage and analyze cyber tips, maintain data quality,

4010
03:12:32,740 --> 03:12:35,940
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and turn information into actionable investigative leads.

4011
03:12:37,380 --> 03:12:41,560
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: We're also proposing po yung monitoring and evaluation,

4012
03:12:42,040 --> 03:12:43,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: joint trainings,

4013
03:12:43,400 --> 03:12:47,560
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: that will help frontline personnel standardize how they recognize,

4014
03:12:47,800 --> 03:12:51,260
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: report, record, and refer osaig sisaing cases.

4015
03:12:52,400 --> 03:12:57,560
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Establishment of dedicated media and public relations bureau

4016
03:12:57,560 --> 03:12:59,680
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and media partnership forum.

4017
03:13:00,600 --> 03:13:06,140
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: For DepEd po, we are proposing capacity building activities.

4018
03:13:06,360 --> 03:13:09,820
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Kasama po dito yung youth peer-to-peer support facilitator training

4019
03:13:10,140 --> 03:13:13,380
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and training of educators and non-teaching personnel.

4020
03:13:13,400 --> 03:13:16,360
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: In osaig and sisaing hotspot areas.

4021
03:13:16,900 --> 03:13:18,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: For Department of Health,

4022
03:13:19,760 --> 03:13:23,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: ito po yung medyo may malaking proposal.

4023
03:13:24,200 --> 03:13:26,100
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: And we have been proposing this for years.

4024
03:13:26,200 --> 03:13:27,940
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: And we'd like to emphasize this again,

4025
03:13:28,460 --> 03:13:33,020
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: which is the 145 million for dedicated multidisciplinary teams

4026
03:13:33,020 --> 03:13:38,160
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: in women and children protection units across 38 DOH retained hospitals.

4027
03:13:38,680 --> 03:13:43,380
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So we emphasize the importance po of,

4028
03:13:43,400 --> 03:13:48,040
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: having a dedicated team including physicians, psychologists,

4029
03:13:48,040 --> 03:13:53,240
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: nurse and medical social worker providing coordinated medical psychosocial

4030
03:13:53,240 --> 03:13:58,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and social work support alongside appropriate legal referrals and follow-up care.

4031
03:13:59,400 --> 03:14:06,100
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: For DSWD po, we are proposing a total of 28.56 million,

4032
03:14:06,100 --> 03:14:13,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: which covers basic course on anti-osaig that aims to strengthen foundational competencies of social workers,

4033
03:14:14,000 --> 03:14:15,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and case managers.

4034
03:14:15,900 --> 03:14:17,400
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Ayan po yung aming presentation.

4035
03:14:17,400 --> 03:14:18,500
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Thank you po for sharing.

4036
03:14:20,700 --> 03:14:24,800
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Ayan po, sa DSWD kasama din po doon yung project safe capacity building,

4037
03:14:25,200 --> 03:14:31,500
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: establishment and enhancement of four child advocacy centers

4038
03:14:31,500 --> 03:14:34,500
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and joint wellness programs for frontline officers.

4039
03:14:35,300 --> 03:14:39,900
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Next po is for Council for the Welfare of Children.

4040
03:14:40,640 --> 03:14:42,940
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Dito po, big bulk dito ay,

4041
03:14:42,940 --> 03:14:46,940
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: focus po of child participation po,

4042
03:14:46,940 --> 03:14:50,940
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: kasama po yung mga bata sa pagbubuo ng IEC materials,

4043
03:14:50,940 --> 03:14:56,440
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: paggawa ng AdvoCom plan and SBCC planning workshop with children and adult,

4044
03:14:56,440 --> 03:14:59,940
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and yung pag-rollout po ng Makabata Helpline 1383.

4045
03:15:00,000 --> 03:15:18,120
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Makaimportante po nito dahil yung Makabata Helpline 1383 po ang ito po yung it aims to improve awareness of the helpline as a reporting and referral channel and connect families and communities to appropriate services.

4046
03:15:18,120 --> 03:15:34,000
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Dahil nung nagkaroon po kami ng mga consultations, ang sinasabi po ng mga bata ay importante po sa kanila na meron silang mapagre-reportan or mapagsusumbungan in case na meron pong mga victims ng abuse, exploitation, and violence.

4047
03:15:36,140 --> 03:15:48,000
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Next po is for DILG, NACC, and NCIP, a total combined amount of 3.6 million po which includes improved systems.

4048
03:15:48,120 --> 03:15:55,220
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: and protocols for OSAEM and SISAEC case identification, referral management, and monitoring.

4049
03:15:55,400 --> 03:15:59,840
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So yung pag-train po ng mga LGUs on case management and referral system.

4050
03:15:59,840 --> 03:16:17,840
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Users training on ASO for NACC and Maraco and capacity building po for IP communities including children po na makasama po sila sa capacity building on improved capacity.

4051
03:16:18,120 --> 03:16:27,240
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Next po, ito po yung summary lang po nung aming mga proposals.

4052
03:16:27,240 --> 03:16:35,740
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So ito po ay katuwang po ng mga agencies na kasama po namin sa NCC OSAEC-SISAEM and we've already shared this with them as well po.

4053
03:16:36,300 --> 03:16:42,960
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Yung sa tingin po namin na dapat i-prioritize dahil po yung ating strategic plan ay until 2028 na lang po.

4054
03:16:42,960 --> 03:16:47,960
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: And we're hoping na by 2027 ay magkaroon po ng sapat na pono.

4055
03:16:48,120 --> 03:16:53,060
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Para magawa po itong ating mga PPAs under the strategic plan.

4056
03:16:54,680 --> 03:17:05,560
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So next po is yung, ito po meron po kaming 5 PPAs outside ng costed implementation plan na we think are also important po to include sa ating budget.

4057
03:17:05,880 --> 03:17:14,760
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So beyond the costed implementation plan, we think that these are essential to address child protection and mental health needs.

4058
03:17:14,760 --> 03:17:17,760
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Yung ilan po dito, I think na-mention na rin po kanina.

4059
03:17:18,120 --> 03:17:20,520
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So i-re-reiterate ko na lang po siya.

4060
03:17:20,680 --> 03:17:25,580
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So in child-friendly and accessible mental health support service amounting to 4 billion.

4061
03:17:26,640 --> 03:17:36,540
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Kasama din po yung nabanggit ko na kanina na women and children protection units in 38 DOH-retained hospitals amounting to 145 million plus.

4062
03:17:37,440 --> 03:17:43,020
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: And then ito po ay budget restoration of the NCC against OSAEC-SISAEM.

4063
03:17:43,020 --> 03:17:47,740
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: And sinare din po sa amin ng sekretaryat na may sinentong letter dito.

4064
03:17:48,120 --> 03:17:55,420
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: May visa office po ninyo for the request to restore po yung kanila pong budget from 2026.

4065
03:17:55,540 --> 03:17:57,440
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So additional 70 million po yun.

4066
03:17:58,220 --> 03:18:03,640
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Of course, budget restoration and augmentation po ng child protection program sa DepEd naman po ito.

4067
03:18:04,340 --> 03:18:09,080
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Na maibalik po yung budget line item na child protection program.

4068
03:18:09,700 --> 03:18:14,620
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Kasi po sa ngayon ay nasubsume na po siya sa learner support program nila.

4069
03:18:14,620 --> 03:18:16,860
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: And ang amount po din is 44 million.

4070
03:18:18,120 --> 03:18:26,780
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Ito din po wish list ng 68 additional plantelia positions for the NCC-OSAEC-SISAEM sekretaryat amounting to 41 million pesos.

4071
03:18:27,680 --> 03:18:35,660
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So ayan po yung summary po yung kabuuan po nung aming pong request na 4.4 billion pesos po.

4072
03:18:35,820 --> 03:18:44,660
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So I'd like to end my presentation po by saying po again na ang bata ang bida sa budget at pera ng taong bayan ay dapat para sa taong bayan.

4073
03:18:44,660 --> 03:18:48,080
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: So sana po maisip niyo na ito ay wish list.

4074
03:18:48,120 --> 03:18:52,520
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Hindi lamang ng mga nakakatanda pero ng mga bata din po lalo na po ngayong Pasko.

4075
03:18:52,780 --> 03:18:53,120
World Vision Advocacy Specialist Pauline Navarro: Thank you.

4076
03:18:54,020 --> 03:18:54,620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

4077
03:18:55,120 --> 03:18:56,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next is sa Unang Hakbang Foundation.

4078
03:18:58,440 --> 03:19:01,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Miss Mary Ayin Padoga.

4079
03:19:01,680 --> 03:19:02,340
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Ayin po.

4080
03:19:02,400 --> 03:19:02,800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ayin.

4081
03:19:03,620 --> 03:19:04,100
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Yes po.

4082
03:19:04,520 --> 03:19:05,460
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Good afternoon everyone.

4083
03:19:05,820 --> 03:19:11,060
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Good afternoon po honorable senators who are here as well as all the CSOs po nandito.

4084
03:19:11,060 --> 03:19:17,300
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So Unang Hakbang is an operating foundation that provides remedial classes in reading math.

4085
03:19:18,120 --> 03:19:24,740
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: For children at risk of dropping out of school, living in the poorest or poorer sections of Mandaluyong and Pampanga.

4086
03:19:25,540 --> 03:19:38,500
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Issues that confront us daily and which impact how children learn are hunger, malnourished, lack of water and proper sanitation and inability of parents to support their children's learning.

4087
03:19:38,500 --> 03:19:47,600
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: These same issues are among those that have limited country's progress on the 2030 Sustainable Development Goals.

4088
03:19:48,120 --> 03:20:01,500
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So ang sa Unang Hakbang lang po ay magbibigay lang po kami ng tatlong recommendations for this session.

4089
03:20:01,780 --> 03:20:04,500
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So yung una po ay yung hunger and malnutrition.

4090
03:20:04,500 --> 03:20:14,260
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So we recommend na sana po ay may restoration of 26 budget of dev ed for school based feeding program.

4091
03:20:14,860 --> 03:20:18,000
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Or to 26 billion from 11.4 billion.

4092
03:20:18,120 --> 03:20:19,460
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: As now proposed.

4093
03:20:19,460 --> 03:20:40,720
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Yung pangalawa naman po ay yung provision of 300 million in DA budget for the research and initial implementation of a nutrition sensitive agricultural program and an agricultural supply chain network centered on bringing produce to areas near families and schools.

4094
03:20:41,500 --> 03:20:45,480
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Yung pangalawang issue naman po ay yung bullying and learners mental health.

4095
03:20:45,480 --> 03:20:47,140
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So narinig po natin no?

4096
03:20:47,140 --> 03:20:55,880
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Hindi lang po talaga kumbaga pabata ng pabata ang may issue or usapin na patungkol sa mental health.

4097
03:20:56,580 --> 03:21:08,120
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So hindi ko na i-explain why kasi it's really issues that we are really encounter right now.

4098
03:21:08,120 --> 03:21:17,120
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So yung recommendation lang po namin is the provision of 300 million for learners welfare intended to strengthen child protection.

4099
03:21:17,140 --> 03:21:23,680
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: And the training of all teachers and students to recognize peers who might need help.

4100
03:21:24,440 --> 03:21:33,140
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: The aim is to initially address the need of the 10,000 that EDCOM 2 has identified as lacking even an anti-bullying policy.

4101
03:21:34,660 --> 03:21:45,860
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: And another one is the provision of another 300 million to support inset training on a positive parenting in schools to create a more just in a peaceful environment in campuses.

4102
03:21:47,140 --> 03:22:02,420
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: And another issues naman po ay yun nga hindi din matutulungan ang mga bata kung hindi din natin i-train or hindi tayo sama-sama para magkaroon ng peaceful environment ang mga bata sa Pilipinas.

4103
03:22:02,420 --> 03:22:10,420
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So ito naman po ay nag-focus sa SDG 4, SDG 5, and SDG 16 ay ang yung adult education and lifelong learning.

4104
03:22:11,820 --> 03:22:17,000
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So ito it's all in its house EST or education and skill training.

4105
03:22:17,140 --> 03:22:33,240
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: And for implementers, DepEd reporting that 2017, there were at least 19 million adults or 18 to 59 years old, comprising a third of that age group who had not completed their basic education.

4106
03:22:33,240 --> 03:22:45,240
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: In the quality basic education development plan, on DepEd underscored that need the strong collaboration involving all education stakeholders from national institutions.

4107
03:22:47,140 --> 03:22:52,520
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: From public to central, public to private, and most notably teachers, parents, and children.

4108
03:22:53,260 --> 03:23:01,580
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: The entire nation must work together to deliver better quality basic education for all and contribute to inclusive economic growth in the Philippines.

4109
03:23:02,340 --> 03:23:14,320
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So through that, our recommendation is the restoration of the line item for community learning centers to house alts and lifelong learning classes.

4110
03:23:14,320 --> 03:23:16,320
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: And also annual allocation.

4111
03:23:17,140 --> 03:23:24,920
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: For the construction of CLCs, 200 million until all municipalities have at least one CLC.

4112
03:23:25,880 --> 03:23:42,380
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: Specified that local government support fund or LGSF may be also used to finance the construction of CLCs and the training of women as para-counselors to support effort to eliminate bullying and improve the mental health of students.

4113
03:23:42,380 --> 03:23:46,760
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: And 100 million honoraria for volunteers who teach in CLCs.

4114
03:23:47,140 --> 03:23:57,840
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: And the CLCs also take notice not just for learning, this is also a safe space for children, for youth, and even for the parents.

4115
03:23:58,020 --> 03:24:00,300
Unang Hakbang Foundation Program Manager Mary Aieen Padoga: So I think that's all po. Thank you.

4116
03:24:00,300 --> 03:24:01,660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

4117
03:24:02,100 --> 03:24:05,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next, for INET Philippines.

4118
03:24:05,420 --> 03:24:16,660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next, for INET Philippines.

4119
03:24:17,140 --> 03:24:22,240
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Sen. J.B. Ejercito, Chairperson of the Senate Committee on Finance.

4120
03:24:23,300 --> 03:24:30,320
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Sen. Fanpilo Lacson, Co-Chair ng Finance Committee.

4121
03:24:31,680 --> 03:24:36,420
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: At ang ating Senate President, Wyn Gatchalian.

4122
03:24:37,300 --> 03:24:41,020
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: At mga kasama sa Civil Society Organizations.

4123
03:24:42,060 --> 03:24:45,980
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: At maging ang aking kasama rin sa INET Philippines.

4124
03:24:47,140 --> 03:24:51,040
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Na walang iba, kundi ang aming Advocacy Officer, Mercy Chan.

4125
03:24:51,860 --> 03:24:53,500
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Magandang hapon po sa inyong lahat.

4126
03:24:54,540 --> 03:24:58,140
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Sen. J.B. Batang San Juan.

4127
03:25:00,700 --> 03:25:05,640
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Ang Education Network for INET Philippines.

4128
03:25:07,640 --> 03:25:13,580
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Isang pambansang koalisyon na binubuo po ng 100 organizations.

4129
03:25:13,780 --> 03:25:16,040
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: More than 100 organizations nationwide.

4130
03:25:16,040 --> 03:25:21,000
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Advocating for inclusive, equitable, quality education for all.

4131
03:25:21,000 --> 03:25:30,500
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: At siya po ang lead organizations education cluster ng Alternative Budget Initiative under Social Watch Philippines.

4132
03:25:31,480 --> 03:25:43,140
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: At nagpapasalamat po kami sa Senado for this opportunity to present our recommendations on the House-approved FY2027 General Appropriations Bill.

4133
03:25:44,080 --> 03:25:46,000
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Our central message is,

4134
03:25:46,040 --> 03:25:54,400
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: education cannot be declared a national priority while essential programs remain unfunded.

4135
03:25:55,080 --> 03:26:02,300
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Legal mandates lack adequate resources and marginalized learners continue to be left behind.

4136
03:26:02,860 --> 03:26:07,040
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: While the House government maintains a substantial allocation for education,

4137
03:26:07,700 --> 03:26:12,000
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: what matters is not only how much government spends,

4138
03:26:12,000 --> 03:26:15,880
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: but where resources go, who benefit,

4139
03:26:16,040 --> 03:26:21,480
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: and whether the budget addresses persistent inequalities in education.

4140
03:26:22,540 --> 03:26:28,300
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Based on our review of the House GAAP and INET's Alternative Budget Proposal,

4141
03:26:28,720 --> 03:26:32,860
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: we urge the Senate to address four priorities.

4142
03:26:34,000 --> 03:26:41,420
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: First, restore and expand funding for inclusive education and lifelong learning.

4143
03:26:41,420 --> 03:26:45,400
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Ang krisis edukasyon na hindi lamang tumutukoy.

4144
03:26:45,400 --> 03:26:48,400
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Sa mga batang nasa loob ng paaralan,

4145
03:26:49,080 --> 03:26:55,340
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: kundi sa mahigit na sampung milyon na mga bata at kabataan na wala sa paaralan.

4146
03:26:55,900 --> 03:27:03,720
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: At gayon din, mahigit sa labing siyam na milyon adults who missed out of education.

4147
03:27:04,780 --> 03:27:11,840
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Ang panawagan pong ito namin, natin, dapat po'y walang naiiwan.

4148
03:27:11,980 --> 03:27:13,660
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: No one left behind.

4149
03:27:15,400 --> 03:27:21,580
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: We acknowledge the House increases for special needs education in SNED,

4150
03:27:22,400 --> 03:27:25,480
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: indigenous people education, and madrasa education.

4151
03:27:25,480 --> 03:27:34,980
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: However, these allocations remain below their FY2026 levels and fall short of what is needed.

4152
03:27:35,960 --> 03:27:39,400
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: INET proposes P2.393 billion for SNED.

4153
03:27:40,060 --> 03:27:45,380
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Kung titignan po natin, noong 2026, it's P1.040.

4154
03:27:45,400 --> 03:27:52,760
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: P2.393 billion na bawasan to support schools, operationalize inclusive learning resource centers,

4155
03:27:53,260 --> 03:27:58,180
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: strengthen child find, and provide accessible learning materials and support services.

4156
03:27:58,940 --> 03:28:02,300
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: For the alternative learning system and lifelong learning,

4157
03:28:02,880 --> 03:28:11,160
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: the House GAAP retains P3.849 billion under the broader Flexible Learning Options Program.

4158
03:28:11,160 --> 03:28:15,020
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: But, a dedicated ALS allocation,

4159
03:28:15,020 --> 03:28:16,800
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: remains unclear.

4160
03:28:17,560 --> 03:28:23,680
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: E-Net proposes P5.55 billion to expand ALS access,

4161
03:28:23,680 --> 03:28:25,680
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: flexible learning,

4162
03:28:25,680 --> 03:28:28,420
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: for working adults and community learning centers,

4163
03:28:28,760 --> 03:28:31,040
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: especially in underserved areas.

4164
03:28:31,560 --> 03:28:37,620
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: We call for P5 billion in dedicated funding for last mile and GHIDA schools

4165
03:28:37,620 --> 03:28:42,120
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: and adequate support for indigenous and Madrasa education.

4166
03:28:43,480 --> 03:28:44,280
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: We urge the Senate

4167
03:28:44,280 --> 03:28:45,020
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: We urge the Senate

4168
03:28:45,020 --> 03:28:50,480
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: protect, and effectively implement funding for the ARAL program

4169
03:28:50,480 --> 03:28:55,620
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: and appropriations must translate into actual tutoring and learning recovery

4170
03:28:55,620 --> 03:28:59,220
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: for struggling learners with funded tutors,

4171
03:28:59,700 --> 03:29:01,560
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: clear implementation targets,

4172
03:29:02,120 --> 03:29:05,340
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: and transparent reporting on delivery and results.

4173
03:29:06,220 --> 03:29:09,060
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: So, our second proposal,

4174
03:29:09,660 --> 03:29:13,180
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: restore and strengthen program-supporting learners' nutrition,

4175
03:29:13,180 --> 03:29:15,900
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: protection, and well-being.

4176
03:29:16,520 --> 03:29:24,080
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: The House GAAP retains 11.431 billion for the screening program,

4177
03:29:24,600 --> 03:29:32,760
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: substantially below the 25.695 billion allocation in FY2026.

4178
03:29:33,700 --> 03:29:40,220
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: ENET proposes 42.295 billion to restore existing funding,

4179
03:29:40,220 --> 03:29:43,140
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: expand feeding to 2 million additional learners,

4180
03:29:43,180 --> 03:29:46,320
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: and strengthen program delivery.

4181
03:29:47,960 --> 03:29:54,780
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: And then, we call for dedicated funding for comprehensive school safety,

4182
03:29:55,620 --> 03:29:59,560
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: child protection, school mental health, and education in emergencies.

4183
03:30:00,000 --> 03:30:10,680
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Beyond physical security, schools need prevention and response system for bullying, violence, abuse, discrimination, and disasters,

4184
03:30:11,300 --> 03:30:17,400
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: accessible reporting and referral mechanisms, trained personnel, and psychosocial support.

4185
03:30:17,980 --> 03:30:27,580
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Funding must support a whole school, inclusive and rights-based approach, not merely new mandates without implementation resources.

4186
03:30:27,580 --> 03:30:34,400
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Third, adequately fund teachers' welfare, school personnel, and inclusive teaching.

4187
03:30:34,800 --> 03:30:41,600
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: We urge the Senate to address continuing shortages of teachers, school principals, and administrative personnel.

4188
03:30:42,380 --> 03:30:52,020
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: ENET proposes funding for 14,274 additional teaching positions, additional principals, and administrative officers,

4189
03:30:52,380 --> 03:30:56,200
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: and 4.8 million for teaching overload compensation.

4190
03:30:56,200 --> 03:31:04,240
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: We also call for full funding of the Magna Carta benefits, including special hardship allowances,

4191
03:31:04,860 --> 03:31:09,220
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: transfer and deployment support, and teachers' mental health services.

4192
03:31:10,260 --> 03:31:17,240
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Actually, RA 4670 is still in problem.

4193
03:31:17,800 --> 03:31:22,500
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: The correct implementation and full implementation of the Magna Carta.

4194
03:31:23,000 --> 03:31:25,580
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Senator Ping and Chair.

4195
03:31:26,200 --> 03:31:29,660
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: No, we would like to ask your support for this.

4196
03:31:29,660 --> 03:31:39,260
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Further, we propose 340 million for positive discipline in everyday teaching with disability inclusion perspective.

4197
03:31:40,300 --> 03:31:49,460
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Training for 100,000 teachers initially to strengthen positive discipline and inclusive disability responsive teaching.

4198
03:31:50,240 --> 03:31:55,660
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Quality education requires teachers whose rights are respected, well-protected, and professionalized.

4199
03:31:56,200 --> 03:31:58,260
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Educational needs adequately supported.

4200
03:31:59,200 --> 03:32:05,980
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Fourth, strengthen financing for early childhood education and underserved regions, particularly BARM.

4201
03:32:06,300 --> 03:32:11,620
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: We call for adequate investments in supplementary feeding, child development centers,

4202
03:32:11,920 --> 03:32:16,840
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: and professionalization and fair compensation of child development workers and teachers.

4203
03:32:17,460 --> 03:32:22,700
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: For BARM, we propose targeted investments in ALS community learning centers,

4204
03:32:22,700 --> 03:32:26,000
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: mobile teachers, early childhood facilities,

4205
03:32:26,200 --> 03:32:33,380
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: and learning recovery with resources directed to the most disadvantaged and conflict-affected communities.

4206
03:32:33,380 --> 03:32:41,220
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Finally, we urge the Senate to ensure transparency, accountability, and equity in budget realignments.

4207
03:32:41,860 --> 03:32:48,080
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Low fund utilization should not automatically be equated with low demand or divinish need.

4208
03:32:48,600 --> 03:32:55,200
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: It may reflect procurement delays, inadequate institutional capacity, and implementation bottlenecks

4209
03:32:55,200 --> 03:32:56,180
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: that governments may face.

4210
03:32:56,200 --> 03:33:03,380
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: The government must address, not use as justification for reducing essential education allocations.

4211
03:33:03,860 --> 03:33:08,720
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: We therefore urge the Senate to scrutinize house budget realignments,

4212
03:33:09,180 --> 03:33:15,160
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: ensure clear program-level allocations, and protect resources for marginalized learners.

4213
03:33:16,020 --> 03:33:17,400
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Honorable Senators,

4214
03:33:18,320 --> 03:33:21,380
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: INET Philippines calls on the Senate

4215
03:33:21,380 --> 03:33:26,080
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: 1. to restore cuts to essential education programs,

4216
03:33:26,200 --> 03:33:30,900
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: expand investments or address persistent education inequalities,

4217
03:33:32,220 --> 03:33:34,660
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: earmark and fund the mandates.

4218
03:33:34,920 --> 03:33:40,080
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Kung kailan marami tayong mga batas na naipasa, bumaba ang budget.

4219
03:33:40,660 --> 03:33:42,900
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Halimbawa lang po ng mga mandates natin.

4220
03:33:43,320 --> 03:33:47,420
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: RA 11510, Alternative Learning System Act.

4221
03:33:48,360 --> 03:33:51,180
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: 11650, Inclusive Education Act.

4222
03:33:51,180 --> 03:33:56,180
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: RA 12313, Lifelong Learning Development Framework.

4223
03:33:56,800 --> 03:34:00,680
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: And then, 12321, Last Mile Schools Act.

4224
03:34:00,680 --> 03:34:05,560
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: And RA 4670, Magna Karta for Public School Teachers.

4225
03:34:06,400 --> 03:34:15,460
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Protect education equity by prioritizing learners and communities facing the greatest barriers.

4226
03:34:16,040 --> 03:34:25,540
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: We respectfully submit our detailed alternative budget proposals for consideration in the Senate's amendment to the FY2027 GAP.

4227
03:34:26,200 --> 03:34:29,940
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: The challenge is not simply to maintain a large education budget,

4228
03:34:29,940 --> 03:34:37,940
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: but to ensure that every peso advances the right to inclusive, equitable, and quality education for all,

4229
03:34:38,280 --> 03:34:43,440
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: especially those who have been historically underserved and left behind.

4230
03:34:43,800 --> 03:34:50,560
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Kaya nga po, pondo para sa karapatan ng mga mag-aaral sa edukasyon at edukasyon para sa lahat.

4231
03:34:51,240 --> 03:34:55,880
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Mula sa INET Philippines, Education Network Flora Arillano,

4232
03:34:56,200 --> 03:34:59,480
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: presidente ng organisasyon na ito.

4233
03:35:00,020 --> 03:35:00,980
E-Net Philippines National Executive Board Member Prof. Flora C. Arellano: Maraming salamat po.

4234
03:35:01,120 --> 03:35:05,220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Maraming salamat po, Professor Flora Arillano.

4235
03:35:06,160 --> 03:35:14,880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next is Mr. Humphrey Soriano from Center for Youth Advocacy.

4236
03:35:15,980 --> 03:35:19,440
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Good afternoon, Mr. Chairperson and Honorable Members of the Committee.

4237
03:35:19,880 --> 03:35:24,060
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Along with the CSOs, maraming salamat po sa oportunidad para makapagsalita.

4238
03:35:24,600 --> 03:35:25,780
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Ako po si Humphrey Soriano.

4239
03:35:26,200 --> 03:35:28,100
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Sa Amplify Education Budget Initiative,

4240
03:35:28,100 --> 03:35:30,600
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: the Budget Campaign of Multiply-Ed Philippines,

4241
03:35:30,700 --> 03:35:34,580
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: ito po ay proyekto ng Center for Youth Advocacy and Networking at Government Watch,

4242
03:35:34,940 --> 03:35:38,360
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: supported by Education Out Loud ng Global Partnership for Education.

4243
03:35:38,880 --> 03:35:43,500
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Ang aming budget initiative po ay ang tanging youth-led education budget initiative in the country.

4244
03:35:44,020 --> 03:35:47,140
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Simple lang po ang panawagan namin ngayong taon para sa education budget,

4245
03:35:47,620 --> 03:35:51,840
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: fix the gaps, fund the margins, and push for an inclusive education budget.

4246
03:35:52,660 --> 03:35:55,940
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Ang kaibahan po namin, we have capacitated,

4247
03:35:55,940 --> 03:35:57,880
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: youth monitors all around the country.

4248
03:35:58,040 --> 03:36:00,660
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: We are present in nine areas all around the Philippines.

4249
03:36:00,860 --> 03:36:06,540
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: And nakita namin sa citizen monitoring namin na meron pa rin tayong kinakaharap na kisi sa edukasyon.

4250
03:36:07,400 --> 03:36:12,280
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: The House approved 987 billion pesos sa new appropriations for DepEd's budget.

4251
03:36:13,060 --> 03:36:16,280
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Ito po ay mas bababa ng 6 billion pesos kesa sa kanilang proposal

4252
03:36:16,280 --> 03:36:19,900
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: at 50 billion pesos na mas bababa sa 2026 budget.

4253
03:36:20,620 --> 03:36:25,200
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Karamihan po dito ay nanggaling sa cut on laptops in classrooms.

4254
03:36:25,940 --> 03:36:30,140
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Ilan po sa mga agenda namin ay ang una, raise the alarm.

4255
03:36:30,560 --> 03:36:35,420
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Hindi po pareho ang guard sa harap ng school at guidance counselor sa loob ng mga paaralan.

4256
03:36:36,000 --> 03:36:38,080
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: Mental health and child protection in the NEP,

4257
03:36:38,780 --> 03:36:43,100
Multiply-Ed Representative Humphrey Soriano: in the NEP, both the Mental Health and Guidance Counseling Program and Child Protection

4258
